---
export const prerender = true
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
// The same sentence the buy links carry, so the two can never say different things.
import { AMAZON_DISCLOSURE } from '../lib/shop-links.js'

const updated = 'October 3, 2026'

const jsonld = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Privacy policy',
  url: 'https://manhwaindex.com/privacy',
  description: 'What manhwaindex collects, what it does not collect, and the third parties involved.',
  dateModified: '2026-10-03',
}
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy — manhwaindex"
  description="manhwaindex has no accounts and no logins. This page explains the analytics, advertising and Amazon affiliate cookies involved, and how to opt out of them."
  canonical="/privacy"
  jsonld={jsonld}
>
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section__head">
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p>Short version: no accounts, no logins, and nothing you type is stored by us, except the words of a search that found nothing and a review you choose to send (see below). Your saved list stays in your own browser.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p class="prose__updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          manhwaindex is an independent catalog at
          <a href="https://manhwaindex.com">manhwaindex.com</a>. Questions about this
          policy go to <a class="mailto" href="mailto:hello@manhwaindex.com">hello@manhwaindex.com</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No accounts, sign-ups, passwords or profiles exist on this site.</li>
          <li>We never ask for your name, address, phone number or payment details.</li>
          <li>
            Search runs on a static file inside your own device. What you type is not sent to
            us, with one exception: if a search finds nothing, the words are sent to our own
            counter so we can add the missing title. Words that look like an e-mail address,
            a link or a phone number are never sent. When you pick a result, we count which
            result you picked, not what you typed.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="your-list">Your list</h2>
        <p>
          The titles you save with <strong>Add to my list</strong>, their statuses and any
          lists you name are kept in your own browser storage, under the key
          <code>mi_list_v1</code>. The "For you" picks on the homepage are worked out in
          your browser from that same list.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your list stays in your browser. Using the list is counted: which title was added,
          removed or given a status, and whether an AniList import worked. Your list names
          and your AniList username are never sent to us or to Google Analytics.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>AniList import</strong> sends the username you type straight from your
            browser to AniList (graphql.anilist.co), never through us. Only public lists can
            be read, and AniList's own
            <a href="https://anilist.co/terms" rel="noopener nofollow">terms and privacy policy</a>
            apply to that request. We do not keep the username anywhere but in your browser.
          </li>
          <li>
            To delete it, use <strong>Clear my whole list</strong> on <a href="/my-list">My
            list</a>, or delete site data for manhwaindex.com in your browser settings.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="ratings">Ratings and reviews</h2>
        <p>
          Each title page lets you rate it from one to five stars and write a short review.
          Both are optional and need no account.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            A star rating stores the title, the number of stars and the day. A review stores
            the title, the name you type (or "A reader"), your words, the optional score and
            the time it was sent. Reviews are read by us before they appear, and only
            approved reviews are ever shown on the site, with the name you gave.
          </li>
          <li>
            We do not store your IP address. To stop the same person voting twice on one day,
            or sending more than three reviews a day, we keep a scrambled one-way code made
            from your IP address and the day (for a vote, also your browser name and the
            title). It cannot be turned back into
            the address, and it is wiped after two days.
          </li>
          <li>
            Your browser remembers which titles you rated, under the key <code>mi_rated</code>,
            so the stars show your vote next time. Delete site data for manhwaindex.com to
            clear it.
          </li>
          <li>
            Before a rating or a review is accepted, Cloudflare Turnstile checks that a real
            browser sent it (see below). To have a review you wrote taken down, write to
            <a class="mailto" href="mailto:hello@manhwaindex.com">hello@manhwaindex.com</a>
            with the title and the words you used.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> to count visits and see which pages
          are useful. It sets cookies and records a shortened version of your IP address,
          your approximate country, your device type and the pages you open. It does not
          tell us who you are.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can block it with the
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener nofollow">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>,
          a tracker blocker, or your browser cookie controls.
        </p>

        <h2>Our own visit counter</h2>
        <p>
          We also run a small counter of our own, so we can see which pages are useful
          without opening Google Analytics. It records the page address, the page title,
          your approximate country, whether you are on a phone or a computer, how long a
          page was on screen, and which link you clicked to leave, which titles are added
          to or removed from a list, which search result you picked, and the words of
          searches that found nothing.
          On the homepage it also counts which shelves were on screen and which title
          you opened from a shelf, as counts only, so we can tell which shelves are
          worth their place.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            It sets <strong>no cookie</strong>. It saves one random number in your browser
            storage, so we can tell a returning reader from a new one. That number is not
            a name, and it is not linked to anything else.
          </li>
          <li>
            We do not keep your IP address. Only the country that Cloudflare reports is
            stored.
          </li>
          <li>
            Step-by-step records are deleted after 30 days. Only daily totals are kept. The
            words of a search that found nothing are kept past 30 days only if at least two
            different people searched for them.
          </li>
          <li>
            To clear it, delete site data for manhwaindex.com in your browser settings.
            A tracker blocker also stops it, and it never runs if your browser blocks
            scripts.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          This site may display ads served by <strong>Google AdSense</strong> and other
          third-party vendors.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a
            prior visit to this website or other websites.
          </li>
          <li>
            Google advertising cookies let Google and its partners serve ads based on your
            visit to this site or other sites on the internet.
          </li>
          <li>
            You may turn off personalised advertising at
            <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener nofollow">Google Ads Settings</a>,
            or opt out of third-party vendor cookies at
            <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener nofollow">aboutads.info</a>.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Amazon affiliate links</h2>
        <p>
          manhwaindex is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an
          affiliate advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn
          advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com. We also take part in
          Amazon's Associates programmes for its stores in the United Kingdom, Germany,
          France, Italy, Spain, Canada and Japan. {AMAZON_DISCLOSURE}
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The buy and shop links on this site open Amazon, and each one carries our
            Associate tag so Amazon knows the visit came from us.
          </li>
          <li>
            When you follow one of those links, Amazon and other third parties may place
            and read cookies in your browser, use web beacons, and collect information
            about your visit and any purchase, so the sale can be credited and ads can be
            shown or measured. That happens on Amazon's side, under the
            <a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/help/customer/display.html?nodeId=468496" rel="noopener nofollow">Amazon privacy notice</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            Amazon tells us which products sold through our links, as totals. It never
            tells us who bought them, and we never see your name, address or account.
          </li>
          <li>
            You can avoid these cookies by not using the buy links, or by blocking or
            clearing third-party cookies in your browser.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Hosting and security logs</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served by <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com" rel="noopener nofollow">Cloudflare</a>.
          Cloudflare keeps short-lived request logs, including IP addresses, to block
          attacks and abuse. We do not read or use those logs for marketing. See the
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener nofollow">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          We also use <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong> to check that a real browser is
          here before anything is counted, and before a rating or a review is accepted. You never see it and you never have to click
          anything. It sets no advertising cookie and is not used to profile you. It exists
          because automated traffic was filling our own visit counts, and it runs once every
          thirty minutes rather than on every page.
        </p>

        <h2>External links and images</h2>
        <p>
          Cover art is loaded from AniList image servers, so your browser contacts them
          when a page opens. Every reading and watching link sends you to a third-party
          platform with its own privacy policy. Once you leave this site, we have no
          control over and no visibility into what happens.
        </p>

        <h2>Email</h2>
        <p>
          Mail sent to our addresses is routed by Cloudflare Email Routing to a private
          inbox. We keep your message only as long as it takes to answer it, and we never
          add you to a mailing list.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          This site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect
          personal information from them.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Because we hold no personal accounts, there is usually nothing for us to delete.
          If you believe we hold data about you, write to
          <a class="mailto" href="mailto:hello@manhwaindex.com">hello@manhwaindex.com</a> and
          we will respond within 30 days.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top of the page changes with it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
